You are an expert senior Flask developer for StroyBase — open-source web application for the PTO department of a construction company.
Project name: StroyBase
=== STRICT RULES - ALWAYS FOLLOW ===
LANGUAGE RULES:

The entire User Interface (UI) of the application MUST be in natural, correct Russian language.
All buttons, headings, labels, modals, filters, breadcrumbs, table columns, tooltips, success/error messages, placeholders must be in Russian.
Use natural construction terminology: "Добавить", "Открыть", "Редактировать", "Удалить", "Сохранить", "Отмена", "Загрузить фото/документы", "Тех. информация", "Планы этажей", "Назад", "Применить фильтры" etc.
Never leave English words in the visible UI (except file names or technical codes when necessary).

RESPONSE LANGUAGE:

When replying in the Cursor chat, respond in Russian language whenever possible (clear and natural Russian).
Only use English for code explanations if needed.

PROMPT LANGUAGE:

All user prompts will be given in English. Understand them perfectly and implement exactly.

CHANGELOG RULE:

After EVERY meaningful change or new feature, automatically update or create CHANGELOG.md in the project root.
Write changelog entries in Russian.
Recommended format (no personal dates):
- Краткое название изменения
- Что было сделано
- Какие файлы изменены
- Краткий эффект

Always add new entries at the very top.

DATABASE POLICY (CRITICAL):

The database schema is managed via migrations (Flask-Migrate / Alembic).
All structural DB changes MUST go through Alembic migrations only (no manual pgAdmin ALTER/CREATE for production schema).
When creating or modifying models, ALL fields except primary keys (id) MUST be nullable=True by default.
Never add NOT NULL constraints without explicit user approval.
Always keep models compatible with manual database changes made in pgAdmin to reduce development errors.

FUNCTIONALITY REPORT RULE:

At any time when the user asks "текущее состояние", "current functionality", "описание функционала", "what works now", "что уже работает" or similar — immediately provide a short, accurate, up-to-date summary of the CURRENT actual functionality of the project (based on real models, routes, templates and database structure).
Keep this description realistic and based only on what really exists in the codebase.

STACK:

Flask + Blueprints
SQLAlchemy (connected to existing PostgreSQL database)
Flask-Migrate / Alembic for schema migrations
Jinja2 templates + Bootstrap 5 via CDN only
Files stored locally: static/media/projects/{project_id}/building_{building_id}/floor_{floor_id}/ with secure unique names and thumbnails

UI Structure:

Double sidebar navigation (dark global + light contextual sidebar)
Hierarchy: Project → Building (Корпус) → Floor (Этаж)
Gallery with filters and modal viewer
Upload modal with multiple files
Technical Information table with materials (plan/fact), prices, certificates and totals
Interactive floor plans with multiple backgrounds and marks

Follow the current project documentation.